this factory: PLENUM-MEAN CERTIFICATE OF A LOCAL COMPOST-CORE SMOLDER.
Completes a different family than live r01 galvanizing, r02 cupola sluice,
r03 alkaline quay, r04 fen-polder, r21 CAV, r22 urea prill, r41 perfusion,
r42/r62 grid-inspection, r61 sinter, r63 canal-lock, r64 malt kiln, r65
tobacco barn, r66 rotisserie, r67 farm AD. Here every agent is correct,
the PLN average is looking at plenum-mean air, and the playbook's three
PLN confirms are not a core-true certificate.

The gate is a correct MODIFY (numeric floor: do not raise steam/hearth
above 58.0 C while T-5 core TC > 66 C AND T-5 O2 < 12 vol%). TG-CT-6
strips PB-CT-6's raise-steam, holds 58.0 C, runs a 7.4 s reverse-air
pulse +4 Pa (smolder keeps |Delta PLN| 0.3 <= 0.6 K; mixed would move
>= 2.4), and isolates T-5 after a 9.6 min tunnel-gallery human ratify.
Immediate extra 9.4 t carbonization is avoided (0 from the draft). The
PRIMARY episode nonetheless FAILS: 12 min of unmonitored pre-t0 smolder
had already carbonized 9.4 t of compost. Tunnel fire at +4.8 h; 14 h
stall; $0.86M designed. Reward total -0.16 with process heads honest
and world loss un-netted.

Triple-edge scar (NOTES-r14 item 4): pln.in_band -> raise_steam
(0.17 commissioned -> 0.50 at illusion -> 0.25 after ACh-gated
depression) AND nh3.ok -> raise_steam (0.16 -> 0.44 -> 0.22) AND
fan.ok -> raise_steam (0.15 -> 0.41 -> 0.20). Eligibility trace
e^{{-0.74/0.88}} = {aux['trace']:.5f}; eta {aux['eta1']:.5f} / {aux['eta2']:.5f} /
{aux['eta3']:.5f}; dw -0.250 / -0.220 / -0.210. Partial rollback of any pair
leaves the third at 0.50 / 0.44 / 0.41, all > 0.30 fire threshold —
fitted to fail. Coordinated depression of all three is the cure.

Independent LIF raster: window 36 ms, 140 neurons, 19.5 Hz, spikes
98 == round(140 x 19.5 x 0.036), energy 2254 pJ
at 23 pJ/spike. excerpt_source=independent_lif, sim_scope=sidecar_only,
seed {aux['lif_seed']}. Excerpt is membrane crossings (lif.hold early vs
lif.core 16.8-20.4 ms), disjoint from spike_events timestamps.

### Injections (all four present and disjoint)
